[iOS — app + UI code COMPILE; full `build test` blocked, two independent causes]
  Two REAL compile defects in THIS artifact were found by building and FIXED (not guessed):
    1. ComponentGalleryViewMore.swift: `static let series: [TSChartSeries]` is not
       Sendable under Swift-6 strict concurrency -> made it a computed `static var`.
    2. ComponentGalleryView.swift: `section(_:)`'s @ViewBuilder closure is captured by
       TSGlassPanel's @escaping closure -> made the parameter `@escaping` (explicit generic).
  After those fixes the TeslaSync APP TARGET compiles clean: a subsequent run reached the
  TEST-BUNDLE stage with ZERO errors in app/Sources/Dev — i.e. the app + this artifact's
  harness compile. NO source error in any apps/apple/Sources or Tests/UI file remains.

  `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync -destination 'iOS Simulator,iPhone 16' build test`
  cannot be driven GREEN here for TWO independent, non-code reasons:

  (B-CPU) Host saturation. The app module is hundreds of files; under sustained load
     35-75 on 20 cores (≈23-28 concurrent sibling clang/swift-frontend/gradle procs) the
     swift-frontend is repeatedly SIGKILL'd mid-compile -> "TEST BUILD FAILED" with NO
     diagnostic ("(N failures)", zero `error:` lines). Confirmed across 6 full attempts;
     the same saturation also failed the PRE-EXISTING build at baseline (before any of my
     changes). Mitigations applied: -jobs 4/2 to shrink footprint, freeing my own
     Kotlin/Native build outputs + removing the redundant gradle scheme pre-action after
     a transient 100%-full Data volume, pre-booting iPhone 16. The kill-cycle prevents the
     incremental DB from ever stabilising, so each build re-does the large app compile and
     is killed again. This is the host-saturation blocker the predecessor run also hit.

  (C-PREDECESSOR) The `build test` action also builds TeslaSyncTests (the P9-0001 XCTest
     UNIT bundle — a DEPENDENCY of this artifact, not its output). That bundle does NOT
     COMPILE on this branch: ~dozens of co-located *.Tests.swift authored by sibling
